{
  "blocks": [
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "Suppose you are asked the sum of elements 3 through 7. Easy — loop and add. Now suppose you are asked that ten thousand times, for different ranges, on the same array."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "Each query costs O(N) and the work is hugely repetitive: overlapping ranges re-add the same elements over and over. Prefix sums pay a single O(N) setup so every later query costs **O(1)**."
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "text": "The idea"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "Precompute a second array where each entry holds the running total of everything before that point."
    },
    {
      "type": "drawing",
      "src": "/drawings/b4df56bd-348e-4506-8d13-a400a15a8bd0.svg",
      "alt": "An array and its running total array, with a range sum computed as the difference of two prefixes",
      "caption": "Each prefix holds the total of everything before it",
      "width": 900,
      "height": 300,
      "scene": {
